<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bartolomé Mitre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1821–1906</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bartolomé Mitre was an Argentine general, historian and statesman. As a leader of the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> he defeated the Argentine Confederation at Pavón in 1861 and reunited the country, serving as president from 1862 to 1868. He built national institutions and railways, led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> in the War of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/triple-alliance-1882">Triple Alliance</a> and founded the newspaper La Nación.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bartolome-mitre.jpg" alt="Bartolomé Mitre" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bartolom%C3%A9_Mitre_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
